# meal_app – Flutter conventions

## Code style (enforced by analysis_options.yaml)
- Single quotes, trailing commas, `const` constructors/declarations wherever possible.
- No `print`; no unawaited futures; explicit return types; `final` locals.
- Strict analyzer (strict-casts/inference/raw-types): never use implicit `dynamic`.
- Keep imports ordered; prefer `package:` imports over relative imports outside the same folder.

## Structure
- Feature-first layout under `lib/`: `lib/features/<feature>/{data,domain,presentation}`, shared code in `lib/core/`.
- Prefer small widget classes over helper methods that return widgets.
- Use `Theme.of(context)` / `ColorScheme` — no hardcoded colors or text styles in widgets.
- Don't call `BuildContext` after an `await` without a `mounted` check.
- State management: not chosen yet — ask before introducing one.

## Workflow
- After changes run `dart format .`, `flutter analyze --fatal-infos`, and `flutter test`; fix everything before finishing.
- Add or update widget/unit tests alongside new behavior (tests mirror `lib/` under `test/`).
- Never edit generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`) or `pubspec.lock` by hand.
- Add dependencies with `flutter pub add`; the Flutter version is pinned in pubspec.yaml — don't bump it casually.
- CI only runs format/analyze/test; app build/release automation is intentionally deferred.
